---
import Icon from "@/components/Icon.astro";
const points = [
  {
    title: "A scope you can actually compare.",
    text: "What stays, what goes, which finishes, and what is excluded. Get those details on the table before comparing the bottom-line price.",
  },
  {
    title: "A plan for an operating property.",
    text: "Vacant units, resident access, material deliveries, and shared spaces all affect the job. Talk through the site conditions before setting the sequence.",
  },
  {
    title: "A clear way to handle changes.",
    text: "Hidden damage and changed selections can affect cost and timing. Agree on how changes will be priced and approved before they become extra work.",
  },
];
---

<section class="approach-section section-padding">
  <div class="container-main approach-grid">
    <div class="approach-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">The way we look at it</p><h2>
        A renovation is more than<br /><em>a good after photo.</em>
      </h2><p>
        It’s the unit you need back. The residents still living next door. The
        budget you have to explain.
      </p><p>
        That’s where the conversation starts. With the work, the constraints,
        and what a finished job needs to look like for you.
      </p><a href="/about" class="text-link"
        >Get to know our approach<Icon /></a>
    </div>
    <div class="approach-points">
      {
        points.map((point, i) => (
          <div class="approach-point">
            <>
              <span>0{i + 1}</span>
              <div>
                <>
                  <h3>{point.title}</h3>
                  <p>{point.text}</p>
                </>
              </div>
            </>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
